# Pinned from the real red run of 2026-08-08 with the injection applied.
#
# The injection is not a revert of the round. The round's centrepiece is that
# the errno policy is written ONCE next to `RecoveryClaimError`, and deleting
# the policy would only prove that deleted code is absent. It KEEPS the policy
# and restores what each of the FOUR LEAVES OUTSIDE ROUND FOUR'S HAND-DRAWN
# BOUNDARY did with a failure:
#
#   F1   `ClaimDirectory::read_regular` maps every non-NotFound open error to
#        `CorruptClaim` — the bucket the resolver QUARANTINES on
#   F1b  `ClaimDirectory::open` does the same for a component-open error, which
#        is a statement about EVERY claim under the directory
#   F2   `ClaimDirectory::names` breaks out of its `readdir` loop on NULL and
#        returns `Ok(a complete directory)`
#   F5   `authority_key` probes with `exists()` instead of `try_exists`, so an
#        unstattable token answers "absent" and MINTS a replacement
#
# Three of the four fixtures are REAL: chmod 000 on the claim file, on the
# per-project claim directory, and on the token's parent directory. Only F2 uses
# a seam, and it reproduces the syscall's exact observable shape — an
# errno-bearing NULL — never the decision that follows it.
exit: 101

# ===== A FAILED FILE OPEN, READ AS A CORRUPT FILE =========================
#
# F1, the block-ship state, RUNNING rather than derived — the review said
# plainly it built no reproduction for this. A live PENDING claim, one `EACCES`
# reading it. `Missing` is the whole finding in one word: the resolver
# quarantined the claim, and for a pending claim there is no committed
# `RecoveryOrigin` to reconstruct from, so the claim is simply GONE. The next
# POST sees a complete origin enumeration plus no claim and reaches
# `plan_pending_recovery_claim` — an observation failure destroyed authority and
# issued permission to mint a competitor beside a running rescue.
contains: an EACCES on the claim file must be unobserved, got Missing

# F1b, the same collapse one level up and wider: `ClaimDirectory::open` speaks
# for every claim under the directory, and one failed `openat` called them all
# corrupt.
contains: an EACCES opening the claim store must be unobserved: Err(CorruptClaim)

# ===== A FAILED DIRECTORY READ, READ AS A COMPLETE DIRECTORY ==============
#
# F2, the block-ship state, RUNNING, on the PRODUCTION boot routing predicate.
# `readdir` returns NULL at end-of-directory AND on error, and the loop cleared
# no errno and read none. `Invalid` here means "no pending recovery owns this
# session", which is the FAIL-OPEN direction: `reattach_live_runs_on_boot`
# reattaches on exactly that answer and `Supervisor::reattach` appends
# `Reattach` into the immutable prefix the pending recovery owns. That write is
# not undoable; a skipped reattach is retried on the next boot.
contains: a mid-listing EIO must not be reported as a complete directory, got Invalid

# ===== AND THE TEST THAT COULD NOT FAIL ===================================
#
# F5. Every `authority_key` test injected through `authority_key_fault`, which
# returns BEFORE control reaches the existence probe — including the five-case
# behavioural pin — so the whole suite stayed green with `exists()` restored.
# This fixture uses NO hook: it removes search permission from the token's
# parent so the real `stat` fails while the token bytes survive. Under the
# injection `exists()` answers `false`, `load_or_generate` is REACHED, and a
# fresh token invalidates every `authority_tag` on the host.
contains: an unstattable token must be unobserved, got Err(CorruptClaim)

# FOUR failures out of thirty-nine. The thirty-five that stay green are the
# point:
#
#   - `the_recovery_authority_types_cannot_spell_failure_as_a_decided_negative`
#     — THE STRUCTURAL PIN — stays GREEN, deliberately. This injection changes
#     which VARIANT the code constructs, not the shape of any type. A red pin
#     here would mean the pin has started measuring behaviour and stopped
#     guarding structure, which is how round three's pin came to pass on the
#     defect it existed to forbid.
#   - every regression rounds one through four shipped stays GREEN, including
#     `no_observation_failure_on_the_authority_path_confirms_or_destroys`, the
#     round-four behavioural pin. It is blind to all four leaves above, which is
#     why there was a round five.
#
# A binary that collapses wholesale, a fifth failure, or a red in the structural
# pin or in any earlier round's regression, is a different failure and has not
# reproduced what this artifact claims.
contains: test result: FAILED. 35 passed; 4 failed
